    {
      "id": 51,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "title": "READ FIRST — inputs / preview / final",
      "pos": [
        40,
        -510
      ],
      "size": [
        1290,
        510
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 11,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# MILLIE / SOURCE REEL / ORIGINAL AUDIO\n1. Upload persona photo in 01 and reel in 02. The workflow contains no media.\n2. Default trim: first 73 frames at 24 fps (about 3.04 s). frame_load_cap=124 is about 5.17 s. skip_first_frames chooses the start at the forced 24 fps. Keep select_every_nth=1. For a whole short clip use frame_load_cap=0. Do not load a long reel for the first test.\n3. Prompt 03 is a generic starting point. Identify the specific target when multiple women appear. Picture 1 = persona appearance, Video 1 = source actions/scene. It is not a first-frame lock. Body proportions are requested, not guaranteed.\n4. Run PREVIEW at 0.4 MP. FINAL OUTPUT (08) is MUTED initially. No latent upscale/refine is requested while it remains muted.\n5. When the preview is acceptable, select only FINAL OUTPUT (08), press Ctrl+M to enable it, then Run. Keep seed, inputs, prompt and preview resolution unchanged. Same-session ComfyUI cache can reuse the first pass; after restart/cache eviction it may run again. This graph does not save a persistent latent checkpoint.\n6. Return FINAL OUTPUT to muted with Ctrl+M when testing more previews. Do not use Bypass/Ctrl+B on samplers. Final size is controlled by 06 (default 1 MP).\nOriginal source audio feeds BOTH exports. There is no generated audio decoder. The audio VAE is only for source conditioning. If a clip has no audio and the loader reports an error, disconnect its audio from the conditioning and export nodes.\nThe internal reference is padded to the H3 frame grid; both outputs are cropped to the actual loaded source frame count. FPS conversion is to 24 fps without intentional time-stretch. Check lip-sync against the original; source audio alone cannot guarantee generated articulation.\nNeeds current ComfyUI, VideoHelperSuite, and LBH latent upscaler. Model names/links are in MODELS_AND_SETUP.md. No SAM3 mask is present in this LBH-based workflow; it regenerates the whole frame.\nValidated graph structure only; no RunPod/GPU render has been performed."
      ]
    }
